WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.113 --> 00:00:01.530
SPEAKER: With an
increasing number

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:04.710
of heterogeneous services
across cloud and on-premises

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.660
environments,
customers are looking

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:10.650
for consistency in connectivity
and security operations.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:13.260
Customers want to be able to
take a service-centric rather

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.900
than infrastructure-centric
approach to consuming cloud

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.550
services.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.160
When consuming
services, some customers

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.830
wish to avoid exposure of their
data to the public internet

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.680
entirely because of
data security and policy

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.000
requirements.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.540
Introducing Private Service
Connect from Google Cloud,

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.150
allowing you to connect
securely and effortlessly

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:36.540
to Google Cloud Services,
third-party partner services,

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.150
and company-owned
applications, helping

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:42.300
you to focus on consumption
of value-added services

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.660
regardless of the
underlying infrastructure.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.970
With Private Service
Connect, SaaS providers

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:50.640
can deliver value-added
services faster,

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.550
providing a much better
experience for the customer.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:56.850
Consumers can access services
directly and privately

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.160
over Google's backbone network.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.680
Google operates an
extensive private network

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.950
that insulates customer traffic
from the public internet,

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:08.010
extending private transit to
the last mile for customers

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:10.440
who need or want this benefit.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.930
Private Service Connect
creates service end points

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:16.920
in consumer VPCs that provide
private connectivity and policy

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:19.620
enforcement, allowing
you to easily connect

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:23.250
services across different
networks and organizations.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.990
Services can be
consumed directly

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:28.050
in your virtual networks
without requiring middle boxes,

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:31.140
proxies, or other
complex configurations,

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:34.890
simplifying the management
of your cloud architectures.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:37.020
Services consumed on
Private Service Connect

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:39.420
have the same high
performance attributes

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:42.120
as that of traffic
between virtual machines.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:43.980
With this product,
we provide you

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:46.200
an end-to-end means
of connecting to

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.120
and managing services.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.610
Take advantage of Google as
a service-centric network

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.460
solution, allowing you
to reach and satisfy

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.020
your clients' needs.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:57.060
Private Service Connect
enables customers

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:00.130
to easily and securely
access services,

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:03.990
making it a win-win for both
producers and consumers.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:07.410
Visit us at cloud.google.com
to learn more

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:09.900
about getting private access
to your services today.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:12.500
[MUSIC PLAYING]

